+# gnss_passthrough v4.9.14: RX -> (SMI-PI filter) -> TX, in the l_clk domain.
+# The ADC pins above already drive nets; these calls add a branch.
 
-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-# GNSS LOOPBACK (antsdr-fw-patch 0002) BEGIN
-#   gnss_passthrough sits between the AD9361 core's ADC outputs and its DAC
-#   inputs, in the axi_ad9361/l_clk sample domain:
-#     CONTROL[0] pass_en = 0 : the DAC gets the normal DMA/FIR stream, so the
-#                              firmware behaves exactly as before (default).
-#     CONTROL[0] pass_en = 1 : RX samples go straight back out on TX
-#                              (RX1 -> TX1 for the GNSS receiver).
-#   The ADC pins already feed rx_fir_decimator / cpack below; these calls only
-#   add a branch, so DMA capture over IIO keeps working.
-#   The four dac_data_* pins of axi_ad9361 are driven ONLY by gnss_passthrough;
-#   the TX FIR / upack outputs that used to drive them now enter
-#   gnss_passthrough/dma_dac_data_* instead (see below).
-#   Registers at 0x43C1_0000 (0x43C0_0000 is axi_vcxo_ctrl).
-#   Linux side: /usr/sbin/gnss_loopback.
-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ad_ip_instance gnss_passthrough gnss_passthrough
-
 ad_connect axi_ad9361/l_clk gnss_passthrough/clk
 ad_connect axi_ad9361/rst   gnss_passthrough/rst
 
